-- title:
--   Germ of a constant in y is a non-unit on the model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a non-zero element. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$ (the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$), so that the finite chart is $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} C$, and let $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j` of the middle chart into the finite and infinite charts, with structure morphism `toBase R F j` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$, and let $r \in R$ be an element whose image under $R \to C$ lies in $y$. The assertion is that there is a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ whose associated prime ideal is exactly $y$, such that the following holds at the point $z =$ `(ιFin R F j).base y'` of $\mathfrak{X}$ lying under $y'$: the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained by pulling $r$ back along `toBase R F j` (in global sections, using the identification of $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R)$ with $R$) lies in the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$.
--
--   This records, at the level of the two-chart integral model, that a constant from the base which lies in a maximal ideal $y$ of the finite chart algebra becomes a non-unit in the stalk at the corresponding point of the model. It is used to instantiate hypotheses of the form "at every point of the model above a given closed point the uniformiser is a non-unit" in the supersingular/blow-up arguments for modular curves of full level that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_asIdeal_eq_and_germ_mem_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_isMaximal_of_mem.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel

theorem AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_asIdeal_eq_and_germ_mem_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_isMaximal_of_mem
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra R F] (j : F) [Fact (j ≠ 0)]
    (y : Ideal ↥(chartAlgFin R F j)) (hy : y.IsMaximal)
    (r : R) (hr : algebraMap R ↥(chartAlgFin R F j) r ∈ y) :
    ∃ (y' : ↥(XFin R F j)), y'.asIdeal = y ∧
      (((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.germ ⊤ ((ιFin R F j).base y') trivial).hom
          (((toBase R F j).appTop).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv.hom r))) ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.stalk ((ιFin R F j).base y')) := by sorry
